[Term]
id: BAO_0003114
name: assay biology component

[Term]
id: BFO:0000001
name: entity

[Term]
id: BFO:0000002
name: continuant
def: "An entity that exists in full at any time in which it exists at all, persists through time while maintaining its identity and has no temporal parts." []
is_a: BFO:0000001 ! entity
disjoint_from: BFO:0000003 ! occurrent
relationship: BFO:0000050 BFO:0000002 {all_only="true"} ! part of continuant

[Term]
id: BFO:0000003
name: occurrent
def: "An entity that has temporal parts and that happens, unfolds or develops through time." []
is_a: BFO:0000001 ! entity
relationship: BFO:0000050 BFO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! part of occurrent

[Term]
id: BFO:0000004
name: independent continuant
is_a: BFO:0000002 ! continuant
disjoint_from: BFO:0000020 ! specifically dependent continuant
disjoint_from: BFO:0000031 ! generically dependent continuant
relationship: BFO:0000050 BFO:0000004 {all_only="true"} ! part of independent continuant

[Term]
id: BFO:0000015
name: process
is_a: BFO:0000003 ! occurrent

[Term]
id: BFO:0000016
name: disposition
is_a: BFO:0000017 ! realizable entity
disjoint_from: BFO:0000023 ! role

[Term]
id: BFO:0000017
name: realizable entity
def: "A specifically dependent continuant  that inheres in continuant  entities and are not exhibited in full at every time in which it inheres in an entity or group of entities. The exhibition or actualization of a realizable entity is a particular manifestation, functioning or process that occurs under certain circumstances." []
is_a: BFO:0000020 ! specifically dependent continuant
disjoint_from: BFO:0000019 ! quality
relationship: BFO:0000050 BFO:0000017 {all_only="true"} ! part of realizable entity

[Term]
id: BFO:0000019
name: quality
is_a: BFO:0000020 ! specifically dependent continuant
relationship: BFO:0000050 BFO:0000019 {all_only="true"} ! part of quality

[Term]
id: BFO:0000020
name: specifically dependent continuant
is_a: BFO:0000002 ! continuant
disjoint_from: BFO:0000031 ! generically dependent continuant
relationship: BFO:0000050 BFO:0000020 {all_only="true"} ! part of specifically dependent continuant

[Term]
id: BFO:0000023
name: role
def: "A realizable entity  the manifestation of which brings about some result or end that is not essential to a continuant  in virtue of the kind of thing that it is but that can be served or participated in by that kind of continuant  in some kinds of natural, social or institutional contexts." []
is_a: BFO:0000017 ! realizable entity

[Term]
id: BFO:0000031
name: generically dependent continuant
is_a: BFO:0000002 ! continuant
relationship: BFO:0000050 BFO:0000031 {all_only="true"} ! part of generically dependent continuant

[Term]
id: BFO:0000034
name: function
is_a: BFO:0000016 ! disposition

[Term]
id: BFO:0000040
name: material entity
def: "An independent continuant that is spatially extended whose identity is independent of that of other entities and can be maintained through time." []
is_a: BFO:0000004 ! independent continuant

[Term]
id: CHEBI:24431
name: chemical entity
namespace: chebi_ontology
def: "A chemical entity is a physical entity of interest in chemistry including molecular entities, parts thereof, and chemical substances." []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: CL:0000000
name: cell
comment: The definition of cell is intended to represent all cells, and thus a cell is defined as a material entity and not an anatomical structure, which implies that it is part of an organism (or the entirety of one).
xref: CALOHA:TS-2035
xref: FMA:68646
xref: GO:0005623
xref: KUPO:0000002
xref: MESH:D002477
xref: VHOG:0001533
xref: WBbt:0004017
xref: XAO:0003012
is_a: UBERON:0000061 ! anatomical structure
relationship: RO:0002162 NCBITaxon:131567 ! in taxon

[Term]
id: GO:0006091
name: generation of precursor metabolites and energy
namespace: biological_process
synonym: "energy pathways" BROAD []
synonym: "metabolic energy generation" RELATED []
is_a: GO:0008152 ! metabolic process

[Term]
id: GO:0006113
name: fermentation
namespace: biological_process
comment: PMID:38821505 mentions exceptions regarding organic compounds and ETC. Fermentation sub-processes exclude glycolysis to prevent redundancy with the glycolytic pathway.
xref: MetaCyc:Fermentation
xref: Wikipedia:Fermentation_(biochemistry)
is_a: GO:0015980 ! energy derivation by oxidation of organic compounds

[Term]
id: GO:0008150
name: biological_process
namespace: biological_process
comment: Note that, in addition to forming the root of the biological process ontology, this term is recommended for the annotation of gene products whose biological process is unknown. When this term is used for annotation, it indicates that no information was available about the biological process of the gene product annotated as of the date the annotation was made; the evidence code 'no data' (ND), is used to indicate this.
synonym: "biological process" EXACT []
synonym: "physiological process" EXACT []
synonym: "single organism process" RELATED []
synonym: "single-organism process" RELATED []
xref: Wikipedia:Biological_process
is_a: BFO:0000015 ! process

[Term]
id: GO:0008152
name: metabolic process
namespace: biological_process
comment: Note that metabolic processes do not include single functions or processes such as protein-protein interactions, protein-nucleic acids, nor receptor-ligand interactions.
synonym: "metabolism" EXACT []
xref: Wikipedia:Metabolism
is_a: GO:0009987 ! cellular process

[Term]
id: GO:0009987
name: cellular process
namespace: biological_process
comment: This term should not be used for direct annotation. It should be possible to make a more specific annotation to one of the children of this term.
synonym: "cell growth and/or maintenance" NARROW []
synonym: "cell physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "cellular physiological process" EXACT []
synonym: "single-organism cellular process" RELATED []
is_a: GO:0008150 ! biological_process

[Term]
id: GO:0015980
name: energy derivation by oxidation of organic compounds
namespace: biological_process
synonym: "chemoorganotrophy" EXACT []
is_a: GO:0006091 ! generation of precursor metabolites and energy

[Term]
id: IAO:0000003
name: measurement unit label
def: "A measurement unit label is as a label that is part of a scalar measurement datum and denotes a unit of measure." []
is_a: IAO:0000009 ! datum label

[Term]
id: IAO:0000009
name: datum label
def: "A label is a symbol that is part of some other datum and is used to either partially define  the denotation of that datum or to provide a means for identifying the datum as a member of the set of data with the same label" []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: IAO:0000027
name: data item
def: "An information content entity that is intended to be a truthful statement about something (modulo, e.g., measurement precision or other systematic errors) and is constructed/acquired by a method which reliably tends to produce (approximately) truthful statements." []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: IAO:0000030
name: information content entity
def: "A generically dependent continuant that is about some thing." []
is_a: BFO:0000031 ! generically dependent continuant
relationship: IAO:0000136 BFO:0000001 ! is about entity

[Term]
id: IAO:0000078
name: curation status specification
def: "The curation status of the term. The allowed values come from an enumerated list of predefined terms. See the specification of these instances for more detailed definitions of each enumerated value." []
is_a: IAO:0000102 ! data about an ontology part

[Term]
id: IAO:0000102
name: data about an ontology part
def: "Data about an ontology part is a data item about a part of an ontology, for example a term" []
is_a: IAO:0000027 ! data item

[Term]
id: IAO:0000225
name: obsolescence reason specification
def: "The reason for which a term has been deprecated. The allowed values come from an enumerated list of predefined terms. See the specification of these instances for more detailed definitions of each enumerated value." []
is_a: IAO:0000102 ! data about an ontology part

[Term]
id: IAO:0000409
name: denotator type
def: "A denotator type indicates how a term should be interpreted from an ontological perspective." []
is_a: IAO:0000102 ! data about an ontology part

[Term]
id: NCBITaxon:1
is_a: OBI:0100026

[Term]
id: NCBITaxon:10239
is_a: NCBITaxon_Union:0000030 ! cellular organisms or viruses

[Term]
id: NCBITaxon:131567
is_a: NCBITaxon_Union:0000030 ! cellular organisms or viruses

[Term]
id: NCBITaxon_Union:0000030
name: cellular organisms or viruses
is_a: NCBITaxon:1
union_of: NCBITaxon:10239
union_of: NCBITaxon:131567

[Term]
id: PATO:0000001
name: quality
namespace: quality
is_a: BFO:0000020 ! specifically dependent continuant

[Term]
id: PATO:0000033
name: concentration of
namespace: quality
synonym: "concentration" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0000070 ! amount

[Term]
id: PATO:0000070
name: amount
namespace: quality
comment: This term was originally named "presence". It has been renamed to reduce ambiguity. Consider annotating with the reciprocal relation,PATO:0001555, has_number_of. For example, rather than E=fin ray Q=count in organism C=10, say E=organism Q=has number of E2= fin ray C=10.
synonym: "count in organism" RELATED []
synonym: "number" RELATED []
synonym: "presence" RELATED []
synonym: "presence or absence in organism" EXACT []
synonym: "quantitative" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0103000 ! quantitative
relationship: RO:0015012 PATO:0001555 ! reciprocal of has number of

[Term]
id: PATO:0001555
name: has number of
namespace: quality
synonym: "cardinality" RELATED []
synonym: "extra or missing physical or functional parts" EXACT []
synonym: "has or lacks parts of type" EXACT []
synonym: "mereological quality" EXACT []
synonym: "number" RELATED []
synonym: "number of" EXACT []
xref: OBO_REL:has_part
is_a: PATO:0000070 ! amount

[Term]
id: PATO:0001842
name: acidity
namespace: quality
synonym: "pH" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0000033 ! concentration of

[Term]
id: PATO:0103000
name: quantitative
namespace: quality
is_a: PATO:0000001 ! quality

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000000
name: process rate metric
def: "A key process metric that represents a quantitative metric, describing rates or fluxes associated, for instance, wiht growth, product formation, substrate consumption, or respiration, during the process." []
is_a: PREFER:0000078 ! key process metric

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000002
name: fermentation project
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process that consist of a single fermentation experiment or multiple related experiments." []
synonym: "project" EXACT []
xref: OBI_0000066
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000003
name: fermentation experiment
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process that consists of sets of fermentation runs conducted within the same project, all following a shared experimental approach or protocol." []
synonym: "experiment" EXACT []
xref: OBI_0000070
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process
relationship: BFO:0000050 PREFER:0000002 ! part of fermentation project

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000004
name: fermentation run
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation process that is carried out under defined experimental conditions (e.g., temperature, pH, agitation) using a single bioreactor system." []
synonym: "cell culture process" BROAD []
xref: CHMO:0001624
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process
relationship: BAO_0002922 PREFER:0000011 ! fermentation medium
relationship: BFO:0000050 PREFER:0000003 ! part of fermentation experiment
relationship: PREFER:8000006 PREFER:0000014 ! uses bioreactor bioreactor
relationship: PREFER:8000011 PREFER:0000008 ! has cultivation condition cultivation condition
relationship: PREFER:8000015 PREFER:0000012 ! cultures cell cell biocatalyst
relationship: PREFER:8000016 PREFER:0000018 ! has collected offline sample
relationship: PREFER:8000017 CHEBI:24431 ! has measured compound chemical entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000005
name: alkalinity cultivation condition
def: "A cultivation condition that represents the alkalinity related aspects of a fermentation cultivation process, grouping process control varibales and process measurement variables that describe or regulate the pH and buffering state of the cultivation environment." []
is_a: PREFER:0000008 ! cultivation condition

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000006
name: gravimetric feed rate control variable
def: "A process control variable that represents the target rate at which the feed (based on its weight) is added to a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
is_a: PREFER:0000009 ! feed process control variable
relationship: BAO_0002874 uom:g.h-1 ! gram per hour
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000075 ! setpoint of gravimetric feed rate

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000007
name: temperature cultivation condition
def: "A cultivation condition that represents the temperature related aspects of a fermentation cultivation process, grouping process control varibales and process measurement variables that describe or regulate the thermal state of the cultivation environment." []
is_a: PREFER:0000008 ! cultivation condition

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000008
name: cultivation condition
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "An information content entity that represents a set of process conditions, grouping relevant process control variables and process measurement variables, describing the environmental and physicochemical conditions under which cells are cultivated." []
synonym: "fermentation culture condition" EXACT []
xref: EDAM:3724
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
relationship: BFO:0000051 PREFER:0000015 ! has part operational parameter

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000009
name: feed process control variable
def: "A process control variable that defines the feed control of a bioreactor or fermentation system during the process." []
is_a: PREFER:0000037 ! feed medium cultivation condition
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! process control variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000010
name: fermentation culture
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a cell population that is cultivated under controlled environmental conditions supporting a fermentation process." []
comment: Fermentation cultures are used in bioprocesses for various applications including precision fermentation, bioremediation, and production of biofuels and pharmaceuticals.
synonym: "cultured cell population" NARROW [OBI:0100060]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000010 PREFER:0000200 ! has fermentation culture type fermentation culture role

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000011
name: fermentation medium
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of an aqueous mixture of macronutrients, micronturients, and buffering agents that is used to support cell growth, metabolic activity and product formation during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "cultivation medium" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000004 CHEBI:24431 ! has medium ingredient chemical entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000012
name: cell biocatalyst
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a whole living cell that is used as a catalyst for bioproduction, catalyzing a biochemical reaction or transformation through their intrinsec or genetically modified metabolic activity." []
comment: In a biotransformation process or bioprocess, a cell biocatalyst converts substrates (organic or inorganic compounds) into outputs such as products, by-products, and cell biomass. Energy derived from substrate conversion is used for product formation, growth and cellular maintenance.
synonym: "biocatalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "biological catalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "catalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "cell catalyst" EXACT []
synonym: "cell factory" EXACT []
synonym: "microbial cell factory" NARROW []
synonym: "WCB" EXACT OMO:0003012 [DOI: 10.1201/9781003413134]
synonym: "whole-cell biocatalyst" EXACT [DOI: 10.1186/s12934-017-0724-7]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000013
name: taxon
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A quality of one or more biological organisms, as well as of parts of organism pertaining to a biological taxon." [PMID:18586729]
xref: NCBITaxon:1
is_a: BFO:0000019 ! quality

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000014
name: bioreactor
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A device or system that is a material entity designed to support the run of a biological and biochemical process by controlling regulated environmental and cultivation conditions, such as temperature, agitation or nutrient injection at different scales, including lab-scale, pilot plant, and industrial-scale systems." [OBI:0001046]
synonym: "bioreactor system" EXACT []
synonym: "fermenter" NARROW [MSIO:0000167]
xref: OBI:0001046
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000185 ! has bioreactor scale bioreactor scale
relationship: PREFER:8000018 PREFER:0000180 ! has operational mode operation mode

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000015
name: operational parameter
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "An information content entity that represents a set of configurable settings used to operate and control a fermentation process, grouping process control variables and mode dependent parameters that define how cultivation conditions are regulated in a bioreactor or fermentation system during the process." []
comment: Operational parameters may vary depending on the selected fermentation operational mode (e.g. batch, fed-batch, continuous) and are realized through instrument or system configuration.
synonym: "operational setting" BROAD []
synonym: "parameter" BROAD [NCIT:C44175]
xref: REPR:InstrumentSetting
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000016
name: fermentation phase
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A time interval of a fermentation process." []
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process
relationship: BFO:0000050 PREFER:0000004 ! part of fermentation run

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000017
name: phase event
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "An operational intervention set by user that triggers the start or end of the fermentation phase." []
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000018
name: offline sample
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a sample that has been withdrawn from a bioprocess system or bioreactor at a specific time point during the ongoing fermentation run for subsequent offline analysis of various compounds, such as substrates, products, and by-products, and biomass." []
synonym: "collected sample" EXACT []
synonym: "material sample" BROAD [OBI:0000747]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000019
name: temperature setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A process control variable that represents the target temperature value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
synonym: "target temperature" EXACT []
synonym: "target temperature value" EXACT []
synonym: "target Tº" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature reference point" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature reference value" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature setting" EXACT [AFO_/result#AFR:0001255]
synonym: "Tº setpoint" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000007 ! temperature cultivation condition
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! process control variable
relationship: BAO_0002874 PREFER:9000004 ! unit
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000041 ! setpoint of temperature measurement

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000020
name: pH setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A process control variable that represents the target ph value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
synonym: "pH control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "ph control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "ph setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "target pH" EXACT []
synonym: "target ph" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000005 ! alkalinity cultivation condition
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! process control variable
relationship: BAO_0002874 uom:%5BpH%5D ! pH based unit
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000040 ! setpoint of pH measurement

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000021
name: pH base solution
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A liquid material entity with basic (alkaline) properties that is used to increase the pH of a solution or system.\n\nIn a fermentation process, it is added manually or automatically to the fermentation run to control and maintain the pH at the defined setpoint or desired value." []
synonym: "pH control base solution" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000022
name: pH acid solution
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A liquid material entity with acidic properties that is used to decrease the pH of a solution or system.\n\nIn a fermentation process, it is added manually or automatically to the fermentation run to control and maintain the pH at the defined setpoint or desired value." []
synonym: "pH control acid solution" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000023
name: core balance metric
comment: A calculated variable that represents a quantitative metric derived from balance calculations over a process, used to characterize the balance of inputs and outputs within a bioreactor or fermenter system during the process.
synonym: "elemental balance metric" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:9000002 ! process calculated variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000024
name: fermentation medium cultivation condition
def: "A cultivation condition that represents the fermentation medium related aspects of a fermentation cultivation process, grouping process control varibales and process measurement variables that describe or regulate the state of the fermentation medium within the cultivation environment." []
is_a: PREFER:0000008 ! cultivation condition

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000025
name: dissolved oxygen setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A dissolved oxygen process control variable that represents the target dissolved oxygen value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
synonym: "dissolved oxygen setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "DO setpoint" EXACT OMO:0003012 []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen process control variable
relationship: BAO_0002874 uom:%25 ! percent
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000039 ! setpoint of dissolved oxygen measurement

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000026
name: dissolved oxygen cascade level control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A dissolved oxygen process control variable that represents the cascade control system linked to a parameter to achieve the desired dissolved oxygen level within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
comment: For instance, in fed-batch operation mode there could be three different cascade levels. Level 1 involves adjusting the stirrer speed parameter. Level 2 involves adjusting the air flow parameter. Level 3 involves adjusting the oxygen flow parameter.
synonym: "dissolved oxygen control strategy" EXACT []
synonym: "DO cascade level control variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen process control variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000027
name: maximum stirring setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A dissolved oxygen process control variable that represents the target maximum revolutions per minute (rpm) of the bioreactor stirrer to be regulated and or maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
synonym: "maximum shaking speed setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "maximum stirring speed setpoint" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen process control variable
relationship: BAO_0002874 PREFER:7000008 ! revolution per minute
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000054 ! setpoint of stirrer speed measurement

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000028
name: minimum stirring setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A dissolved oxygen process control variable that represents the target minimum revolutions per minute (rpm) of the bioreactor stirrer to be regulated and or maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
synonym: "minimum shaking speed setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "minimum stirring speed setpoint" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen process control variable
relationship: BAO_0002874 PREFER:7000008 ! revolution per minute
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000054 ! setpoint of stirrer speed measurement

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000029
name: pressure cultivation condition
def: "A cultivation condition that represents the pressure related aspects of a fermentation cultivation process, grouping process control varibales and process measurement variables that describe or regulate the pressure state within the cultivation environment." []
is_a: PREFER:0000008 ! cultivation condition

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000030
name: aeration gas type
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A dissolved oxygen process control variable that represents the type of gas used for aeration in a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process, which may include aire or specific gases such as pure oxygen, nitrogen or carbon dioxide." []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen process control variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000031
name: maximum aeration setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A dissolved oxygen process control variable that represents the target maximum rate of at which gas can be supplied to be regulated and or maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
synonym: "maximum aeration setpoint" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen process control variable
relationship: BAO_0002874 uom:L.min-1 ! liter per minute
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000055 ! setpoint of air flow rate

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000032
name: minimum aeration setpoint control variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A dissolved oxygen process control variable that represents the target minimum rate of at which gas can be supplied to be regulated and or maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a process." []
synonym: "minimum aeration setpoint" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000015 ! operational parameter
